Eru Recipe

Ingredients:

500g shredded eru leaves

1kg waterleaf

500g beef

250g cow skin

200g smoked fish

150g dried fish

1 cup ground crayfish

1 cup red palm oil

2 seasoning cubes

Salt to taste

Fresh pepper to taste

Preparation:

Wash the beef and cow skin. Put them in a pot with salt, seasoning cubes, and a little water. Cook until tender.

Wash and chop the waterleaf. Soak dried eru in warm water and rinse thoroughly.

Add the waterleaf to the meat and cook for 5–7 minutes. Add the eru leaves and stir well.

Add the smoked fish, dried fish, ground crayfish, pepper, and palm oil. Mix everything together and cook for 15–20 minutes, stirring occasionally.

Taste and adjust the salt. Cook until the vegetables are tender and the soup is rich and well combined.

Serve hot with water fufu or garri.
